---
description: Review-gated PRD-to-code workflow for frontend repositories
alwaysApply: true
---

When working from product requirements, read `.ai-dev/constitution.md` and `.ai-dev/workflow.md` first. Follow `.agents/skills/prd-to-code/references/coordinator.md` for `next` / implement / review handoff.

Use `.ai-dev/features/<requirement-id>/status.json` as the state machine. Perform only the current `next` action and stop at human review gates. Never self-approve a gate. Do not treat prepare-review/review-delivery contract ok as authorization.

Require source or repository evidence for material claims. Apply the workflow evidence labels and do not implement unresolved inferences, conflicts, contract gaps, unlocated requirements, backend-owned behavior, or work belonging to another repository.

Preserve existing changes. Implement one approved task at a time in the real project recorded by the feature status. Do not automatically commit, merge, push, or deploy. Run the repository verification commands and update the feature's traceability and verification artifacts.

Inspect, modify, run, and verify business code directly in the developer's current project so the Agent and human reviewer use the same local environment. Do not require a Worktree or use artifact links as the execution path. Determine framework, versions, package manager, and commands from the real repository itself.

After implementation, run `node .ai-dev/scripts/record-code-changes.mjs <feature-dir> <file...>` to create the changed-file manifest, live file links, and final patch. Before editing an existing workflow artifact, mark its relative artifact path with `update-consistency.mjs`; refresh the downstream files, then resolve only the files actually updated. Artifact synchronization must not move `status.json.state` backward.

Before presenting a gate, run:

```bash
node .ai-dev/scripts/validate-change.mjs <feature-dir>
```
